Hello Heroes, 

we have a brand-new update for the demo of Forgotten Mines, which will give you a much-better experience of what the final game will play like!

[list]
[*]New UI! 
[*]Several bug fixes;
[*]Better sound effects for click, hover and game texts;
[*]Added textual presentation in each area;
[*]It is now possible to skip the text of events;
[*]6 rooms in each area;
[*]Each area now has a theme song;
[*]A secondary trombone track that increases volume as the player advances in the area;
[*]Animated visuals;
[*]Bosses and Sub-Bosses rebalanced;
[*]Corrected and more informative texts;
[*]Logos and intro texts are now skippable;
[*]Units receive additional AP at level 3 and 5 for free;
[*]With the exception of Healers, no class starts with the same perks or skills;
[*]Snipers now receive Sidestep as their initial skill: they can move up to two tiles on the sides for free, the -cost increases every time it is used and goes back to zero at the beginning of the new turn;
[*]The player can select enemies in the Positioning Phase to see what it is and how much it moves;
[*]When restarting a battle, the player returns from the Positioning Phase;
[*]Abandon Run button (and leave with the gems);
[*]HP bars shown above the player's units; 
[/list]


We hope you'll like this new demo!

And don't forget: Forgotten Mines will be available on [b]Steam later in 2024[/b]! Until then, you can [b]wishlist the game[/b] and play the demo!

https://store.steampowered.com/app/2238630/Forgotten_Mines/

If you want to chat with the team and other players, you can join us on [url=discord.gg/pFreZSEgxQ][b]Discord[/b][/url] and [url=https://twitter.com/forgotten_mines][b]Twitter[/b][/url]!

What's new?! MANY THINGS:

- Bug fixes;
- New Perk: [b]Limit Breaker[/b] -> For each point of Fatigue, gets +3 ATK;
- New Perk: [b]Counter[/b] -> Has 50% to counter a melee damage;
- New Perk: [b]Ethereal Step[/b] -> Has a 50% chance of not spending an Action Point with movement;
- [b]Extra Power[/b] now grants +5 ATK;
- Skill Re-Roll System: When leveling up, the player will have 3 re-rolls during his run to use in skills;
- The number of Enemy Reinforcements when passing the spin limit has been adjusted according to the area of ​​the game where the player is;
- Thief can receive [b]Ethereal Step[/b] at level 4;
- Berserker gets [b]Break Limits[/b] and [b]Counter[/b] at level 2;
- Many other classes and enemies can learn [b]Counter[/b] now;
- Magic Power and Healing Power values ​​are now displayed in the UI;
- Demo general optimization: now the game runs faster and lighter;
- Several new magic items added;

What's new? A lot of things:

- Bug fixes;
- New Perk: [b]Fair[/b] -> When without allies on adjacent tiles, receive a bonus to physical damage;
- New Perk: [b]Unfair[/b] -> When with allies on adjacent tiles, receive a bonus to physical damage;
- New Perk: [b]Metamagic[/b] -> Considerably increases the power of offensive and healing spells;
- New Perk: [b]Surveillance[/b] -> It doesn't cost Action Points to equip an item;
- New action: [b]Nullify[/b] -> Nullifies the opponent's buffs (Power, Rage, Mag Res and Immunity);
- Healing now grants only 0.25 XP;
- All support and status spells now grant 0.25 XP;
- Red Mage, Blue Mage, Green Mage and White Mage can get [b]Metamagic[/b] at some levels;
- Thief can gain [b]Unfair[/b], [b]Surveillance[/b]and [b]Null[/b]throughout his progression;
- The Hunter can receive [b]Fair [/b]and [b]Disable[/b];
- [b]Bear Trap[/b] has been buffed;
- Magic Resistance has been buffed;
- Several new magic items added;

Hello, good people from Steam! Wanna know the new features available on the [i]0.0.5v[/i] of [b]Forgotten Mines[/b]? Check it out:

- [b]4K[/b]: 4K is now available as an option on the Options Menu on Title Screen;
-[b] Change OST Style[/b]: the player can change the Music Style of the game on the Options Menu, on Title Screen. Two Styles are added for now: [i]Dwarven Battle Music[/i] and [i]'JRPG' Nu Jazz[/i];
- [b]Protect[/b] was buffed: when protecting a unit no longer get a status condition from an enemy atack;
- [b]Upgraded Equipments[/b] now shows the attribute that was improved (if there is any);
- [b]Change View[/b] label was added to the Unit Control Manager when the mouse gets in the little square on the left bottom;
- [b]Selling Value[/b] is now showed when shopping, when mouse hovers on the inventory items;
- [b]New Perk added[/b]: [i]Sanctity[/i] is obtainable for [i]lv 2 White Mages[/i] and [i]lv 4 Paladins;[/i]
- [b]New Item added[/b]: [i]Dark Bow[/i], rare item, is now available on the game;
- [b]Bug Fixes[/b];

Just little adjustments on the UI to make the experience of the player better on [b]Forgotten Mines[/b] demo.

- [b]Flammable Warning[/b] on item tooltip. Before the game just showed a tiny little symbol on the superior line. Now, added to that, there is a red "Flammable" label;

- Now, when flammable equipment burn on the middle of the combat, [b]a pop up informs the player what type of equipment has burned away[/b];

- When the player clicks on a button that needed to be holded, a [b]warning shows up to tell the player to hold the button[/b];

- Now, when a unit levels up when still selected, it'll auto deselect;

Hello folks! After some good ideas from the players to improve the quality of life for [b]Forgotten Mines[/b], here is the version [i]0.0.3[/i]. So, what's new on 0.0.3?

- [b]UI/UX change #01[/b]: now the unit don't deselect after an action. It'll keep selected and deselect only the action, turning back to the movement option;
- [b]UI/UX change #02[/b]: A warning will appear one turn before the limit, telling the player the need to go to the next room soon as possible. The "End Turn" button will turn red, telling visually to the player the risk of pressing it;
- [b]UI/UX change #03[/b]: When an item is dragged by the player, a message will appear on the screen, telling the player that there is a cost to equip an item, but not for drink a potion;
- [b]Heal[/b] now gives to the healer 0.5 Experience Points;
- [b]Arrow Attacks[/b] are buffed, a little;

Hi! After some feedback and bug report I made this quick update for the [i]demo version[/i], and I call this the [i]Reto Update[/i] to the version 0.0.2. Let's see what we got here:

- Bug Fixes;
- [b]Heal[/b] is boosted a little bit;
-[b] Goblin Soldier[/b] is a little nerfed;
- The HP of the [b]Boulders[/b] are lowered;[img]
